id: pm-nc94mk
title: "GH-1140: reject ambiguous bare comma tuples for linked file and test mutations"
description: "GitHub issue #1140 proves that update/create --file and linked-test add paths accept a comma-bearing bare value with no structured key before the first comma, persist the entire tuple as path or command, and return success. The result is a linked file that cannot resolve or a linked test that cannot execute, while TOON rendering can make the corruption look like a valid row."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[6]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:sdk",data-integrity,linked-artifacts,parser
created_at: "2026-08-28T19:16:55.859Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-29T16:28:03.171Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-29T16:28:02.328Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-29T16:28:02.328Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: "A shared public SDK parser rejects ambiguous comma-bearing bare file and test entries before mutation with a stable typed refusal and token-efficient keyed/JSON recovery; explicit path= and command= forms preserve literal commas losslessly; create, update, files, test, CLI, SDK, MCP, contracts, completions, and help expose one consistent grammar; health and validation identify legacy corrupted rows without rewriting history; focused unit/integration/packed npm+npx+bun+bunx/temp-workspace acceptance plus literal 100/100/100/100 coverage, docstrings, static, and security gates pass"
definition_of_ready: "All-status duplicate search remains distinct from the closed structured-key, unknown-key, docs-pair, and delimiter-safe removal fixes; the exact accepted grammar is specified before implementation."
goal: project management = context management
objective: "Make every linked file and test mutation lossless, executable, and self-describing across SDK and CLI entry points."
value: Agents can trust a successful linked-artifact write without reopening JSON to detect silent tuple corruption.
impact: Prevents durable false context and permanently unrunnable verification evidence.
why_now: "Issue #1140 reports 38 corrupted items across 16 repositories on versions through 2026.8.28, demonstrating a recurring fleet-wide agent UX failure."
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: high
reporter: GitHub #1140
severity: medium
environment: pm 2026.8.21 through 2026.8.28; Node 26.5.0; Linux
repro_steps: "Run pm update <id> --file \".github/workflows/release.yml,project,the publish step\" or pm test <id> --add \"node scripts/verify.ts,project,120\"; read the item as JSON and observe the entire tuple stored in path or command."
resolution: Restricted linked-artifact assignment classification to the leading CSV segment so trailing structured fields cannot bypass bare-comma refusal.
expected_result: "README.md,scope=project must return bare_comma_entry_ambiguous while valid leading keyed entries and equals-bearing literal paths retain their established behavior."
actual_result: "The leading-segment classifier, regression suite, linked PM tests, temporary-workspace CLI acceptance, full 8,124-test exact coverage, and complete static assurance stack pass. Exact graph verification is traversable through verifies edges to pm-s8cth5 and pm-mlc3."
affected_version: 2026.8.21-2026.8.28
component: SDK linked-artifact input grammar and CLI adapters
regression: false
customer_impact: Agents receive successful writes for unusable context and verification evidence; observed across 38 items in 16 repositories.
